[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
=====================================================================
sysutils/tcreech-containers installed.

On a host that already has hand-maintained files in
%%HOOKSDIR%%, move them aside first; pkg will not quietly
take over files it does not own:

  cd %%HOOKSDIR%%
  for f in children.json children.py linprocfs.json linprocfs.py zfs.json zfs.py; do
    [ -e "$f" ] && mv "$f" "$f.hand-maintained"
  done

Then, once per host:

1. containers.conf has no drop-in directory, so the hooks_dir key must
   be in the live file.  Idempotent, keeps a .orig, prints a diff:

     %%ENABLE%%

2. Reload the resident API process and prove the hooks load.  A missing
   hooks directory is silently ignored and so is a hook that exits
   non-zero, so do not assume -- test:

     service podman_service restart
     podman run --rm --os=linux docker.io/library/debian:latest \
       sh -c 'cat /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/00freebsd && apt-get update -qq && echo apt OK'

3. Hook payload paths are checked when the directory is read, so keep
   every .json and its script in the same package.  If containers stop
   starting, look at the newest .json in %%HOOKSDIR%% first.

%%PREFIX%%/etc/cni/net.d/lan.conflist and the registry trust file are
installed as .sample because they differ per host.  The registry trust
file only needs copying into place; lan.conflist needs a look first,
because its "master" must name an existing bridge(4) carrying the LAN
NIC as a member -- this build says "%%BRIDGE%%", and a plain NIC name is
never valid.  This package does not create that bridge, so give it a
home in rc.conf rather than leaving it to whichever jail starts first:

  sysrc cloned_interfaces+="%%BRIDGE%%"
  sysrc ifconfig_%%BRIDGE%%="addm <lan-nic> up"

A host that runs no LAN-addressed containers can skip lan.conflist
entirely.
=====================================================================
EOM
}
]
